# THE COMPILED ACTOR BINARIES.
#
# `kontra serve` execs `<actor-dir>/<name>` for a Go actor — a compiled binary, not a source
# tree — so building one leaves a ~52MB architecture-specific blob sitting next to its source.
# Five of them is a quarter of a gigabyte, which is not something to carry in git history where
# it can never be removed without a rewrite.
#
# Listed by name rather than by a pattern because the binary is named after its directory and
# gitignore has no way to express "the file with the same name as its parent". A new Go actor
# here needs a new line — the alternative, ignoring every extensionless file, would also hide
# real scripts.
#
# Peer of workspaces/scraping/actors/gocanary/.gitignore, which makes the same argument.
/desync/desync
/dnsfacts/dnsfacts
/linkfind/linkfind
/nscheck/nscheck
/nuclei/nuclei
/subfinder/subfinder
